1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,426
Earning on Bitcoin in Mezo's BTC/MUSD pool takes five steps: a trove,

2
00:00:05,426 --> 00:00:11,018
a borrow, a pool deposit, a gauge stake, and watching your collateral ratio.

3
00:00:11,038 --> 00:00:14,746
mbLP does all five in one deposit.

4
00:00:14,766 --> 00:00:20,565
You put in BTC, the vault borrows MUSD against it, pairs the two in the pool,

5
00:00:20,565 --> 00:00:22,674
and stakes for MEZO rewards.

6
00:00:22,694 --> 00:00:28,202
You hold one token, stay about 1x BTC, and exit any time.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,324
This is version six, live on testnet.

8
00:00:32,344 --> 00:00:34,996
I connect a real MetaMask wallet.

9
00:00:35,596 --> 00:00:40,336
MetaMask opens beside the page, and asks before it connects.

10
00:00:42,877 --> 00:00:45,433
I deposit a thousandth of a bitcoin.

11
00:00:45,453 --> 00:00:48,375
MetaMask shows exactly what I'm signing,

12
00:00:48,375 --> 00:00:51,297
and my shares arrive in one transaction.

13
00:00:51,897 --> 00:00:53,274
The network, the site,

14
00:00:53,274 --> 00:00:57,405
the vault's address and the amount are all there before I confirm.

15
00:00:58,592 --> 00:01:03,806
Right now the testnet pool sits outside the vault's ten percent oracle band,

16
00:01:03,806 --> 00:01:09,020
so the vault keeps new BTC idle, instead of adding liquidity at a bad price.

17
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:11,452
That's the guard, working live.

18
00:01:12,053 --> 00:01:14,225
Exits stay open.

19
00:01:14,245 --> 00:01:18,457
I withdraw half, and the BTC is back in my wallet.

20
00:01:19,057 --> 00:01:24,181
The app simulated this exit first, and MetaMask asks me to confirm it.

21
00:01:26,348 --> 00:01:28,784
Don't trust me, try to break it.

22
00:01:28,804 --> 00:01:32,800
This page fires twelve live attacks at the deployed vault.

23
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:37,416
Eleven are refused, one is harmless, and none gets through.

24
00:01:38,017 --> 00:01:42,493
For Wave two, I worked through the review, then attacked my own vault.

25
00:01:42,513 --> 00:01:46,516
Every fix has a test that failed first: the borrowing cap,

26
00:01:46,516 --> 00:01:50,589
Recovery Mode exits, and a sandwich that paid the attacker.

27
00:01:51,189 --> 00:01:54,177
Testnet only, and unaudited.

28
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:57,449
Try it at mblp.neocities.org.
